          "impression_count": 6343,
          "like_count": 57,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589519955386710",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "5/ The next 4 years, like the last 4 years, will be all about scaling.\n\nMuch of progress depends on our ability to keep scaling compute + data exponentially.\n\nThis is no easy feat. Scaling data + compute will be some of the largest infrastructure projects of our time."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:36.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589519955386710"
        ],
        "id": "1795589519955386710",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 8,
          "impression_count": 9937,
          "like_count": 43,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589518667788711",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "4/ The key insight of scaling laws was actually published earlier that year in Jan 2020 by OpenAI—\"Scaling Laws for Neural Language Models\"\n\nThis paper and GPT-3 ultimately was the start of the current AI era of rapidly scaling language models—especially the compute + data needed"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:36.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589518667788711"
        ],
        "id": "1795589518667788711",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 2,
          "impression_count": 7345,
          "like_count": 42,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 1
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589517421986282",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "3/ @scale_AI had started working on language models the year before on the very first RLHF experiments on GPT-2. But GPT-2 still felt very much like a toy at that time.\n\nGPT-3 was the first moment where it was obvious this would be the major theme of AI"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:36.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589517421986282"
        ],
        "id": "1795589517421986282",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 5,
          "impression_count": 7586,
          "like_count": 45,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589516314734911",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "2/ GPT-3 was when it first became clear what the potential of scaling language models was.\n\nThe efficacy of GPT-3 took the AI community by surprise for the most part—the capabilities were staggering compared to everything that came before in NLP."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:35.000Z",
